      "Ana had worked at the Sunrise Café for two months, and every single shift began the same way: a small knot of fear in her stomach right before the door chimed and the first customer walked in. She could make a perfect cappuccino with her eyes closed. She could work the register faster than anyone else on the morning shift. But the moment a customer asked her a question she didn't expect, her English seemed to disappear completely, like water running out of her hands.",
