      "Her manager, Mr. Whitfield, had noticed. He was an older man with kind eyes and a habit of humming while he wiped down the counters. \"You know,\" he said quietly one slow afternoon, \"your English is better than you think it is. You just say everything so carefully, like you're afraid of breaking it.\"",
