      "The next morning, a young woman came in, clearly in a hurry, glancing at her watch every few seconds. \"I'm running so late,\" she said, half to herself, half to Ana. Instead of just taking the order silently the way she usually would, Ana heard herself say, \"Don't worry, I'll make it quick for you. Rough morning?\" The words came out before she could second-guess them.",
      "The woman looked up, surprised, and smiled. \"You have no idea. My alarm didn't go off.\" \"That's the worst,\" Ana said, already steaming the milk. \"Here, on the house for the wait.\" She slid an extra pastry across the counter. The woman's whole face relaxed. \"Thank you, seriously. You just made my morning so much better.\"",
